## 🎯 Complete Workflow Example

```bash
# 1. Test API connection
curl -X POST "http://34.122.156.88:3001/api/optisigns/config/test" \
-H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"apiToken": "your_optisigns_token"}'

# 2. Save configuration
curl -X PUT "http://34.122.156.88:3001/api/optisigns/config" \
-H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"apiToken": "your_optisigns_token", "settings": {"autoSync": true}}'

# 3. Sync displays
curl -X POST "http://34.122.156.88:3001/api/optisigns/displays/sync" \
-H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN"

# 4. Create content
curl -X POST "http://34.122.156.88:3001/api/optisigns/content" \
-H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"name": "Welcome", "type": "text", "content": "Hello!", "duration": 30}'

# 5. Send content to displays
curl -X POST "http://34.122.156.88:3001/api/optisigns/content/CONTENT_ID/send" \
-H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"displayIds": ["DISPLAY_ID_1", "DISPLAY_ID_2"]}'
```

